\title{mascot: Live Mood-Driven Mascots for 'Shiny' Apps and 'Quarto' Sites}
\description{
Adds a character drawn in code to 'Shiny' apps and 'Quarto' sites. The character shows a mood and animates when the mood changes, follows light and dark mode, and takes its colours from the theme. It works offline: the drawing is done in the browser from bundled 'JavaScript'.
}
\section{Conditions}{

\code{\link[=mascot]{mascot()}} and the helpers raise an error on an invalid value;
\code{\link[=update_mascot]{update_mascot()}} warns instead and leaves the mascot unchanged. All errors raised by
mascot, including checkmate assertions, carry class \code{mascot_error}. Warnings
have class \code{mascot_warning} and messages have class \code{mascot_message}. Invalid
update values also carry \code{mascot_update_ignored}; low contrast carries
\code{mascot_contrast}, and messages about inline placement carry
\code{mascot_placement_ignored}. Checkmate assertion errors keep checkmate's
message, line by line.

Specific error classes are \code{mascot_error_choice} for invalid choices,
\code{mascot_error_dots} for unexpected arguments, \code{mascot_error_argument} for
authoring argument errors, \code{mascot_error_character} for character content
errors, and \code{mascot_error_file} for character file errors.

\code{mascot_palette_dropped} is the warning when a character swap drops a palette
that the new character does not have. Two warnings are for development:
\code{mascot_gesture_dropped} when a pending gesture cannot play, and
\code{mascot_template_evicted} when unused UI templates leave the cache. Each
inherits \code{mascot_warning}.
}

\section{Options}{

\code{options(mascot.contrast_warnings = TRUE)} forces R contrast warnings on;
\code{FALSE} forces them off everywhere. By default they appear only when
\code{\link[shiny:in_devmode]{shiny::in_devmode()}} is \code{TRUE}, and always in \code{\link[=mascot_preview]{mascot_preview()}} and the
studio. Colours are kept unchanged.
}

